        "code": "#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\nmkdir -p reports\n\n# --- Node.js ---------------------------------------------------------\n# Exact install from the lockfile; fails if package.json and the lockfile\n# disagree; dependency install scripts are not executed\nnpm ci --ignore-scripts\n\n# Registry signatures and provenance attestations of what was installed\nnpm audit signatures\n\n# Full report kept as a build artifact, whatever the result\nnpm audit --json > reports/npm-audit.json || true\njq '.metadata.vulnerabilities' reports/npm-audit.json\n\n# The gate: production dependencies only, fail on high and critical\nnpm audit --omit=dev --audit-level=high\n\n# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------\n# Every archive must match a SHA-256 recorded in requirements.txt\npython -m pip install --require-hashes -r requirements.txt\n\n# Audit the same pinned and hashed file, without resolving anything again\npython -m pip install --quiet pip-audit\npip-audit -r requirements.txt --require-hashes --disable-pip\n",
